========================================================================

--- RTL DIFF (what changed in the design) ---
commit 039ab4b338855f53476ffd03a0b143fb36bdb751
Author: Greg Chadwick <gac@lowrisc.org>
Date:   Thu Sep 21 17:09:09 2023 +0100

    [otbn,rtl] Refactor loop control so commit doesn't factor into prefetch
    
    Previously when a loop start was requested but not committed (due to an
    error) this effected the next loop information outputs used by the
    prefetcher to determine what to prefetch. This can cause timing issues.
    
    With this change the next loop information doesn't depend upon the
    commit (it provides what will happen if the commit happens) and breaks
    the paths causing timing issues.
    
    Signed-off-by: Greg Chadwick <gac@lowrisc.org>

