    As discussed in #12429, the KMAC interface actually supports byte
    strobes. Since the ROM controller only reads out 39bit per cycle,
    it therefore makes sense to only transmit 5 bytes worth of data to KMAC
    per cycle instead of a zero padding to the maximum interface with
    and transferring 8 bytes per cycle.
    
    This change should improve the ROM hash time by almost 50%.
    
    Signed-off-by: Michael Schaffner <msf@google.com>

